WEBVTT

00:00:03.262 --> 00:00:07.802
Speaker: <b>American and British English – the same, but different</b>

00:00:09.069 --> 00:00:13.196
American and British people speak the same language – English –

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.727
but with some small differences.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:17.450
<b>1</b>

00:00:17.839 --> 00:00:18.719
<b>Vocabulary</b>

00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:22.132
Some words are different in British English,

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.596
for example, they say <i>postcode</i> not <i>zip code</i>,

00:00:27.237 --> 00:00:32.031
<i>holiday</i> not <i>vacation</i>, and <i>lift</i> not <i>elevator</i>.

00:00:33.211 --> 00:00:35.155
Some words have different meanings,

00:00:35.275 --> 00:00:37.978
for example, in American English,

00:00:38.224 --> 00:00:41.475
<i>potato chips</i> are thin slices of fried potatoes.

00:00:42.071 --> 00:00:45.667
In British English, they are the same as French fries.

00:00:47.123 --> 00:00:47.607
<b>2</b>

00:00:48.012 --> 00:00:48.710
<b>Spelling</b>

00:00:49.911 --> 00:00:54.969
<i>Color</i>, <i>favor</i>, and other words that end in <i>-O-R</i> in American English,

00:00:55.342 --> 00:00:57.975
end in <i>-O-U-R</i> in British English.

00:00:59.062 --> 00:01:05.102
<i>Center</i>, <i>theater</i>, and other words that end in <i>-T-E-R</i> in American English

00:01:05.186 --> 00:01:08.278
end in <i>-T-R-E</i> in British English.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:10.386
<b>3</b>

00:01:10.735 --> 00:01:11.291
<b>Grammar</b>

00:01:12.466 --> 00:01:16.318
There are some small differences, especially prepositions.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.697
For example, British people say <i>at the weekend</i>,

00:01:21.261 --> 00:01:23.600
but Americans say <i>on the weekend</i>.

00:01:25.114 --> 00:01:25.717
<b>4</b>

00:01:26.241 --> 00:01:27.273
<b>Pronunciation</b>

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.555
This is the really important difference between British and American English.

00:01:33.461 --> 00:01:36.592
British accents and American accents are very different.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.222
When British people start speaking,

00:01:39.468 --> 00:01:42.889
Americans know they are British, and vice versa.